    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9042" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνιπτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>unwashen,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χερσὶ δ᾽ ἀνίπτοισιν</span> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ῃσιν</span>
			)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> Διὶ λείβειν . . ἅξομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.266
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				725
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Matt.</u>
				15.20
			</span></i>: prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ποσί,</span> i.e.
				<i>unprepared,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Pseudol.</u>
				4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>not to be washed out,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἷμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1459
				</span></i>
			.</div>
